# Negative test: within the GMN logic plane, the gmeow:gmnAsciiFallback keys are a SECOND
# parseable notation (the ASCII stream a downstream writer/parser must round-trip when the
# Unicode sign is not adopted). Two DISTINCT logic operators/targets sharing one ASCII
# fallback would make that stream ambiguous, so each logic-plane fallback MUST be unique
# across distinct targets. Any returned row is a collision: two candidates with different
# logic: targets declaring the same fallback key.
#
# Two candidates with the SAME target legitimately carry DIFFERENT fallbacks and are never a
# collision; the ?targetA != ?targetB filter keeps the gate to genuine cross-operator key
# clashes. The current logic-plane keys (not, is_subclass_of, implies, is_equiv_to, fa, ex,
# and, or, iff, top, bot, derives, entails, box, dia, concept_and, concept_or, after, btrue,
# bfalse, bboth, bnone, isupp, iopp, iboth, inone) are pairwise distinct across targets, so
# this returns no rows. It mirrors gmn-ascii-fallback-uniqueness.rq (math plane), retargeted
# to the logic: namespace.
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>

SELECT ?fallback ?candA ?candB ?targetA ?targetB WHERE {
    ?candA a gmeow:GmnSymbolCandidate ;
           gmeow:gmnCandidateTarget ?targetA ;
           gmeow:gmnAsciiFallback ?fallback .
    ?candB a gmeow:GmnSymbolCandidate ;
           gmeow:gmnCandidateTarget ?targetB ;
           gmeow:gmnAsciiFallback ?fallback .
    FILTER (STRSTARTS(STR(?targetA), "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/"))
    FILTER (STRSTARTS(STR(?targetB), "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/"))
    FILTER (STR(?candA) < STR(?candB))
    FILTER (?targetA != ?targetB)
}
ORDER BY ?fallback ?candA ?candB
